{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Rn4UWDJwspi4CrYhRxcHjP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#ifndef INCLUDE_REMIMU\n2\t\n3\t/************\n4\t \n5\t    REMIMU: SINGLE HEADER C/C++ REGEX LIBRARY\n6\t\n7\t    Compatible with C99 and C++11 and later standards. Uses backtracking and relatively standard regex syntax.\n8\t\n9\t    #include \"my_regex.h\"\n10\t\n11\tFUNCTIONS\n12\t\n13\t    // Returns 0 on success, or -1 on invalid or unsupported regex, or -2 on not enough tokens given to parse regex.\n14\t    static inline int regex_parse(\n15\t        const char * pattern,       // Regex pattern to parse.\n16\t        RegexToken * tokens,        // Output buffer of token_count regex tokens.\n17\t        int16_t * token_count,      // Maximum allowed number of tokens to write\n18\t        int32_t flags               // Optional bitflags.\n19\t    )\n20\t    \n21\t    // Returns match length, or -1 on no match, or -2 on out of memory, or -3 if the regex is invalid.\n22\t    static inline int64_t regex_match(\n23\t        const RegexToken * tokens,  // Parsed regex to match against text.\n24\t        const char * text,          // Text to match against tokens.\n25\t        size_t start_i,             // index value to match at.\n26\t        uint16_t cap_slots,         // Number of allowed capture info output slots.\n27\t        int64_t * cap_pos,          // Capture position info output buffer.\n28\t        int64_t * cap_span          // Capture length info output buffer.\n29\t    ) \n30\t    \n31\t    static inline void print_regex_tokens(\n32\t        RegexToken * tokens     // Regex tokens to spew to stdout, for debugging.\n33\t    )\n34\t\n35\tPERFORMANCE\n36\t\n37\t    On simple cases, Remimu's match speed is similar to PCRE2. Regex parsing/compilation is also much faster (around 4x to 10x), so single-shot regexes are often faster than PCRE2.\n38\t\n39\t    HOWEVER: Remimu is a pure backtracking engine, and has `O(2^x)` complexity on regexes with catastrophic backtracking. It can be much, much, MUCH slower than PCRE2. Beware!\n40\t\n41\t    Remimu uses length-checked fixed memory buffers with no recursion, so memory usage is statically known.\n42\t\n43\tFEATURES\n44\t\n45\t    - Lowest-common-denominator common regex syntax\n46\t    - Based on backtracking (slow in the worst case, but fast in the best case)\n47\t    - 8-bit only, not unicode\n48\t    - Statically known memory usage (no heap allocation or recursion)\n49\t    - Groups with or without capture, and with or without quantifiers\n50\t    - Supported escapes:\n51\t    - - 2-digit hex: e.g. \\x00, \\xFF, or lowercase, or mixed case\n52\t    - - \\r, \\n, \\t, \\v, \\f (whitespace characters)\n53\t    - - \\d, \\s, \\w, \\D, \\S, \\W (digit, space, and word character classes)\n54\t    - - \\b, \\B word boundary and non-word-boundary anchors (not fully supported in zero-size quantified groups, but even then, usually supported)\n55\t    - - Escaped literal characters: {}[]-()|^$*+?:./\\\n56\t    - - - Escapes work in character classes, except for 'b'\n57\t    - Character classes, including disjoint ranges, proper handling of bare [ and trailing -, etc\n58\t    - - Dot (.) matches all characters, including newlines, unless REMIMU_FLAG_DOT_NO_NEWLINES is passed as a flag to regex_parse\n59\t    - - Dot (.) only matches at most one byte at a time, so matching \\r\\n requires two dots (and not using REMIMU_FLAG_DOT_NO_NEWLINES)\n60\t    - Anchors (^ and $)\n61\t    - - Same support caveats as \\b, \\B apply\n62\t    - Basic quantifiers (*, +, ?)\n63\t    - - Quantifiers are greedy by default.\n64\t    - Explicit quantifiers ({2}, {5}, {5,}, {5,7})\n65\t    - Alternation e.g. (asdf|foo)\n66\t    - Lazy quantifiers e.g. (asdf)*? or \\w+?\n67\t    - Possessive greedy quantifiers e.g. (asdf)*+ or \\w++\n68\t    - - NOTE: Capture groups for and inside of possessive groups return no capture information.\n69\t    - Atomic groups e.g. (?>(asdf))\n70\t    - - NOTE: Capture groups inside of atomic groups return no capture information.\n71\t\n72\tNOT SUPPORTED\n73\t\n74\t    - Strings with non-terminal null characters\n75\t    - Unicode, unicode character classes, etc\n76\t    - Exact POSIX regex semantics (posix-style greediness etc)\n77\t    - Backreferences\n78\t    - Lookbehind/Lookahead\n79\t    - Named groups\n80\t    - Most other weird flavor-specific regex stuff\n81\t    - Capture of or inside of possessive-quantified groups (still take up a capture slot, but no data is returned)\n82\t\n83\tUSAGE\n84\t\n85\t    // minimal:\n86\t    \n87\t    RegexToken tokens[1024];\n88\t    int16_t token_count = 1024;\n89\t    int e = regex_parse(\"[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\", tokens, &token_count, 0);\n90\t    assert(!e);\n91\t    \n92\t    int64_t match_len = regex_match(tokens, \"23.53) \", 0, 0, 0, 0);\n93\t    printf(\"########### return: %zd\\n\", match_len);\n94\t    \n95\t    // with captures:\n96\t    \n97\t    RegexToken tokens[256];\n98\t    int16_t token_count = sizeof(tokens)/sizeof(tokens[0]);\n99\t    int e = regex_parse(\"((a)|(b))++\", tokens, &token_count, 0);\n100\t    assert(!e);\n101\t    \n102\t    int64_t cap_pos[5];\n103\t    int64_t cap_span[5];\n104\t    memset(cap_pos, 0xFF, sizeof(cap_pos));\n105\t    memset(cap_span, 0xFF, sizeof(cap_span));\n106\t    \n107\t    int64_t matchlen = regex_match(tokens, \"aaaaaabbbabaqa\", 0, 5, cap_pos, cap_span);\n108\t    printf(\"Match length: %zd\\n\", matchlen);\n109\t    for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++)\n110\t        printf(\"Capture %d: %zd plus %zd\\n\", i, cap_pos[i], cap_span[i]);\n111\t    \n112\t    // for debugging\n113\t    print_regex_tokens(tokens);\n114\t\n115\tLICENSE\n116\t\n117\t    Creative Commons Zero, public domain.\n118\t\n119\t*/\n120\t\n121\t#include <stdint.h>\n122\t#include <stdio.h>\n123\t#include <stddef.h>\n124\t#include <string.h>\n125\t#include <assert.h>\n126\t\n127\tstatic const int REMIMU_FLAG_DOT_NO_NEWLINES = 1;\n128\t\n129\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_NORMAL      = 0;\n130\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_OPEN        = 1;\n131\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_NCOPEN      = 2;\n132\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_CLOSE       = 3;\n133\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_OR          = 4;\n134\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_CARET       = 5;\n135\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_DOLLAR      = 6;\n136\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_BOUND       = 7;\n137\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_NBOUND      = 8;\n138\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_KIND_END         = 9;\n139\t\n140\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_MODE_POSSESSIVE  = 1;\n141\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_MODE_LAZY        = 2;\n142\tstatic const uint8_t REMIMU_MODE_INVERTED    = 128; // temporary; gets cleared later\n143\t\n144\ttypedef struct _RegexToken {\n145\t    uint8_t kind;\n146\t    uint8_t mode;\n147\t    uint16_t count_lo;\n148\t    uint16_t count_hi; // 0 means no limit\n149\t    uint16_t mask[16]; // for groups: mask 0 stores group-with-quantifier number (quantifiers are +, *, ?, {n}, {n,}, or {n,m})\n150\t    int16_t pair_offset; // from ( or ), offset in token list to matching paren. TODO: move into mask maybe\n151\t} RegexToken;\n152\t\n153\t/// Returns a negative number on failure:\n154\t/// -1: Regex string is invalid or using unsupported features or too long.\n155\t/// -2: Provided buffer not long enough. Give up, or reallocate with more length and retry.\n156\t/// Returns 0 on success.\n157\t/// On call, token_count pointer must point to the number of tokens that can be written to the tokens buffer.\n158\t/// On successful return, the number of actually used tokens is written to token_count.\n159\t/// Sets token_count to zero if a regex is not created but no error happened (e.g. empty pattern).\n160\t/// Flags: Not yet used.\n161\t/// SAFETY: Pattern must be null-terminated.\n162\t/// SAFETY: tokens buffer must have at least the input token_count number of RegexToken objects. They are allowed to be uninitialize