{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_dehotsrqoh5hqibb55spoocuxderzqpm3aat374znvecxajboxka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 39 tests pass with no failures.\n\nSummary of the work:\n\n1. **Read C source** (`my_regex.h`, `my_regex_test.c`, `my_regex_tests.cpp`) and Rust translation (`src/my_regex.rs`).\n\n2. **Built a C harness** to compute ground-truth values for tests across many regex patterns, captures, and edge cases.\n\n3. **Found and fixed a translation bug** in the Rust port: the original `rewind_or_abort` used `Vec::pop()` which actually removes elements, but the C code uses a fixed-size array with a `stack_n` counter where slots remain valid even after \"popping\". Indices stored in `prev` and `q_group_stack` would point past the Rust Vec's length, causing index-out-of-bounds panics. I refactored:\n   - `rewind_stack` is now a fixed-capacity Vec preallocated with default `RegexMatcherState`s.\n   - Added an explicit `stack_n: usize` counter that tracks the logical top.\n   - Updated `rewind_save` and `rewind_or_abort` to manipulate `stack_n` rather than `Vec::push`/`pop`.\n   - Updated all manual stack-manipulation sites and the final capture-walking loop to use `stack_n`.\n\n4. **Wrote 39 tests** in `src/bin/test_my_regex.rs` covering:\n   - Literal matching, dot, character classes, escape classes, escape literals, hex escapes (incl. the documented C bug where `\\xNN` only reads the first nibble twice), whitespace escapes\n   - Anchors (`^`, `$`), word boundaries (`\\b`, `\\B`)\n   - Quantifiers: `*`, `+`, `?`, `{n}`, `{n,}`, `{n,m}`, lazy `?`, possessive `+`\n   - Alternation, capturing groups, non-capturing groups `(?:)`, atomic groups `(?>)`\n   - Captures with the implicit outer group, possessive captures returning -1\n   - Pathological patterns, complex e-mail patterns, `start_i` offsets\n   - Invalid patterns returning `Err(-1)` and buffer-too-small returning `Err(-2)`\n   - Constants, `RegexToken::new/set_mask/check_mask/invert_mask`, `Default`, `RegexMatcherState::new`, `print_regex_tokens` smoke test\n\nFinal result: `cargo test` reports `39 passed; 0 failed`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":160972,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":357,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e298ebc4-2d7e-4a4f-8879-892213f222f9","uuid":"6a9b31cb-2cbd-45be-ab78-a84b6fe1dd12"}
